{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 41, :comments ["<b>The swarming thing upon the earth.</b> To exclude the gnats in pulse and in beans, and the worms in lentils — for they did not swarm upon the earth but within the food; but once they emerged into the air and swarmed, they are forbidden (Sifra; Ḥullin 67)." "<b>It shall not be eaten.</b> To impose liability on one who feeds another as on one who eats. And a thing is not called שֶׁרֶץ unless it is low, short-legged — so that it appears only to crawl and move."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:05:59.104993220Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}